Description: Do not run the channel callback for defaults xfwm4 writes itself
 On a first start the xfwm4 xfconf channel has no properties yet.
 loadXfconfData() writes every default back with xfconf_channel_set_property(),
 which emits "property-changed" on the same channel synchronously, from inside
 loadSettings(): xfconf's cache emits the signal in the very call that sets the
 property (xfconf/xfconf-cache.c, xfconf_cache_set), not from the main loop.
 cb_xfwm4_channel_property_changed() then reloads the settings recursively (15
 loadSettings() calls instead of 1 on a clean profile) and, for
 "use_compositing", calls compositorActivateScreen() -> compositorManageScreen()
 before loadSettings() has stored vblank_mode. The compositor starts with
 vblank_mode == VBLANK_OFF: neither GLX nor XPresent vsync, so windows tear.
 init_compositor_screen() then calls compositorManageScreen() a second time,
 which finds _NET_WM_CM_S<n> owned by xfwm4's own window and logs "Another
 compositing manager is running on screen 0"; XFWM4_COMPOSITING_MANAGER is
 never acquired.
 The defaults are applied from rc[] when loadXfconfData() returns, so block
 the callback while they are written.
 .
 Reproduced in a trixie container (Xvfb + xfce4-session, fresh HOME): the
 warning on the first start and not on the second, gone with this patch; a
 channel that lacks only use_compositing triggers it as well.
 Upstream status: not yet reported. The code is unchanged in xfwm4 master
 (d30886f7b, 2026-10); no issue in gitlab.xfce.org/xfce/xfwm4, Debian's BTS or
 Launchpad matches (searched 2026-10-03).
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/src/settings.c
+++ b/src/settings.c
@@ -214,6 +214,21 @@
 loadXfconfData (ScreenInfo *screen_info, Settings *rc)
 {
     gint i;
+
+    /*
+       Writing a default back to the channel makes xfconf emit "property-changed"
+       on this very channel, synchronously, from within xfconf_channel_set_property().
+       cb_xfwm4_channel_property_changed() would then reload the settings
+       recursively and, for "use_compositing", start the compositor, while
+       loadSettings() is still running: before vblank_mode is loaded, so with
+       no vsync, and before init_compositor_screen(), which then finds the
+       compositor selection already owned by xfwm4 itself.
+       The defaults are applied from rc[] when this function returns, so the
+       callback has nothing to do for these writes.
+     */
+    g_signal_handlers_block_by_func (screen_info->xfwm4_channel,
+                                     cb_xfwm4_channel_property_changed,
+                                     screen_info);
     for (i = XPM_COLOR_SYMBOL_SIZE; rc[i].option; ++i)
     {
         gchar *property_name = g_strconcat("/general/", rc[i].option, NULL);
@@ -238,7 +253,9 @@
         }
         g_free(property_name);
     }
-
+    g_signal_handlers_unblock_by_func (screen_info->xfwm4_channel,
+                                       cb_xfwm4_channel_property_changed,
+                                       screen_info);
 }
 
 static int
